## Verification Harness

Gates are **run, not assumed**. A task is done when the gates covering it have been
executed and observed to pass — quote the real output; never infer success from a
command that printed nothing.

- `scripts/harness/gates.sh quick` — cheap checks; also runs automatically when a
  session ends and **blocks** if red.
- `scripts/harness/gates.sh full` — the real Definition of Done. Minutes, not
  seconds. Run it once, deliberately, not from a hook.
- `scripts/harness/check-file.sh <path>` — lint one file; runs automatically after
  every edit and blocks on failure.

Full details, including what each gate actually runs on this target, are in
**`AGENTS-HARNESS.md`** at the repo root.

**If a gate was already red before you started**, say so and name the ticket — do not
silently skip it, and do not claim work is done on top of it.
